From aa12587cc574c8c29c2c108cb368533775d06dd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:16:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Wallguard: fetch once the WAN and clock are up; Update per
 list; AdGuard sinkhole rules (102.8 line)

- Boot: a router rebooting at 03:00 showed ads until the 05:15 run. The boot-time update ran
  before the WAN (nvram's WAN state is stale until start_wan) and before the clock (TLS refuses
  every list host on the boot clock), every fetch failed, and a list that failed beside one that
  came down was never owed. Now nothing is fetched until a default route exists and the clock is
  set; the pending mark holds the epoch of the next try (0 = at WAN up, else 10 min doubling to 6
  h while any subscribed list has no usable copy); rc's firewall hook, the first NTP sync (ntpd.c,
  the hook this firmware runs; ntp.c for the other client) and the self-monitor call `retry`,
  which fetches only the owed lists; the lists on a USB volume are used under the mark as soon as
  the store attaches (restore_build, wallguard_store_attached).
- update takes a subset: $D/only from httpd (a row's Update button, CGI
  action=update&id=<subscribed feed>) or ONLY from sync and retry; the other lists' state lines
  are carried over and nothing else is fetched. A save that adds a list fetches that list alone.
  The page shows an Update button on every subscribed row (RSHD_183); the safe-search refresh
  stays with the full update.
- wallguardc: `$dnsrewrite=` to one of the five sinkhole targets AdGuard DNS uses is a block (its
  Popup Hosts list is written that way throughout and had read as 0 names); one bar is an exact
  entry, `@@|name^` an exact allow; the 2026-11-03 download gate counts a list's allows, so a
  source made only of exception lines is taken (the Names column reads "N allowed", RSHD_184). The
  host test says `[ -x /bin/nvram ]`: the router's ash had no `command` builtin, and `command -v`
  said "the host" on the router.
httpd/web.c also carries the 64-bit partition sizes of get_usb_info (the USB commit) and
reaper_node_of_sta for the Wireless Log (that commit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
